  "notes": "PaperBench evaluates AI agents on replicating machine learning research papers from scratch. Constructed from 20 ICML 2024 Spotlight and Oral papers, it contains 8,316 individually gradable leaf tasks organized in hierarchical rubrics.\n\nKey characteristics:\n- Agents must replicate research papers autonomously (12-hour time limit, single A10 GPU)\n- Rubrics co-developed with original paper authors\n- LLM judge (o3-mini SimpleJudge) achieves F1 = 0.83 vs human judges at $66/paper\n- Human baseline: 41.4% on a 3-paper subset (best@3, 48 hours)\n- PaperBench Code-Dev variant focuses on code-only replication (o1-high: 43.4%)\n\nTwo agent scaffolds tested:\n- BasicAgent: Simple loop with tool access (generate command → execute → observe)\n- IterativeAgent: Forces models to use full time budget, improves some models\n  (exact IterativeAgent scores not rendered in paper HTML; tables blank due to LaTeX rendering issues)\n\nCode at github.com/openai/frontier-evals. From OpenAI."
}
